🌟 Internship Overview

This repository contains the completed projects and source code from my Data Analytics Internship at CodeAlpha. The internship focused on extracting actionable insights from data, utilizing Python, and applying industry-standard libraries to solve real-world problems.

To successfully complete this program, I have built and documented three comprehensive projects covering Data Engineering, Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA), Data Visualization, and Natural Language Processing (NLP).

📂 Completed Tasks

🌐 Task 1: Web Scraping & Data Engineering

Objective: Automate the extraction of product data from an e-commerce website and structure it into a clean dataset.

Description: Built a custom web scraper using Python to navigate a sandbox bookstore. The script parses HTML DOM trees, extracts specific product details (Titles, Prices, Ratings, Availability), performs immediate data cleaning (handling missing values, formatting strings to floats), and exports a structured CSV file ready for analysis.

Technologies: Python, Requests, BeautifulSoup (bs4), Pandas

Key Skills: Data Extraction, HTML Parsing, Data Cleaning.

🔗 View Task 1 Folder / Code (Update this link to your folder)

📊 Task 3: Data Visualization & Exploratory Analysis

Objective: Transform raw, tabular business data into actionable visual insights for decision-makers.

Description: Conducted Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) on a restaurant transaction dataset. Engineered new financial metrics (such as tip percentages) and generated a professional dashboard of charts. The visualizations identify revenue peaks, map correlations between bill size and tips, and analyze demographic spending habits.

Technologies: Python, Pandas, Matplotlib, Seaborn

Key Skills: EDA, Feature Engineering, Visual Storytelling, Statistical Plotting.

🔗 View Task 3 Folder / Code (Update this link to your folder)

🧠 Task 4: Sentiment Analysis (NLP)

Objective: Apply Natural Language Processing to classify customer reviews and understand public opinion at scale.

Description: Developed a Python script to automatically read e-commerce product reviews and classify the underlying customer emotion as Positive, Negative, or Neutral. Utilized a lexicon-based approach to calculate polarity scores for sentences and visualized the aggregate customer satisfaction levels using a bar chart.

Technologies: Python, NLTK (VADER), Pandas, Matplotlib

Key Skills: Natural Language Processing (NLP), Lexical Analysis, Text Classification.

🔗 View Task 4 Folder / Code (Update this link to your folder)

🛠️ Installation & Setup

To run any of the projects in this repository locally, please ensure you have Python 3.x installed.

Clone this repository:

git clone https://github.com//CodeAlpha_Data_Analytics_Internship.git


Navigate to the project directory:

cd CodeAlpha_Data_Analytics_Internship


Install the required dependencies:

pip install pandas requests beautifulsoup4 matplotlib seaborn nltk


🎓 What I Learned

Through this internship, I significantly strengthened my practical coding skills and analytical mindset:

Data Acquisition: I learned that if data isn't handed to you, you can engineer solutions to scrape it directly from the web.

Visual Storytelling: I learned how to move beyond basic spreadsheets to create visual dashboards that immediately highlight business trends.

Machine Learning Concepts: I gained introductory experience in NLP, teaching a machine how to interpret human emotion through text.

